<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann I Joseph, Prince of Liechtenstein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1760">1760</a>–<a href="/years/1836">1836</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann I Joseph was prince of Liechtenstein from 1805 to 1836 and an Austrian field marshal who fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a> and negotiated the Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a> in 1805. Under him Liechtenstein became sovereign in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a> and then joined the German Confederation; he issued its first constitution in 1818.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-i-joseph-prince-of-liechtenstein.jpg" alt="Johann I Joseph, Prince of Liechtenstein" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Baptist von Lampi the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Josef_I_von_Liechtenstein.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
